NETWORKING DAY 14 NOTES — Project 1: Network Recon Script
Date: 13-10-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- A recon script is the earlier days chained together: sweep (Day 04), quick scan (Days 04-06), saved output (Day 07)
- nmap -sn finds who is alive; -F, -sV, -T4 and --host-timeout make the follow-up scan fast and safe from hangs
- -oA saves three formats at once; the script reads .gnmap (hostnames, open ports) and .nmap (MAC addresses)
- awk can join data from several files into one table; sort -V puts IP addresses in natural order
- Guards in a script (private ranges only, /24 or smaller, retype to confirm) help, but cannot know who OWNS a network
- Always read a script before running it, and confirm the subnet with ip route first
- nmap -F only checks the top 100 ports, so a summary can miss services on unusual ports

